ncr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.0013421141475932485,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":32.9,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.17403280515502811,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.013426067806998749,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":77.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.01075,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.5,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":50.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Howard Hughes Holdings Inc., together with its subsidiaries, develops master planned communities (MPCs) in the United States. It operates through three segments: Operating Assets, MPC, and Strategic Developments. The Operating Assets segment acquires or develops retail, office, and multifamily properties, as well as invests in other real estate properties. The MPC segment plans, develops, and sells land in large scale and long term community development projects to homebuilders and developers. The Strategic Developments segment develops residential condominium and commercial property projects, as well as various other properties. The company was founded in 2010 and is headquartered in The Woodlands, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David R. O'Reilly | CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 500 people. Revenue per employee of $2.9M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 20%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $835K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $40K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Howard Hughes Holdings Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $5.0B market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +37.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $418M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 28 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.73\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 17.4% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 70/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 81% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 57% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.6M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Howard Hughes Holdings (HHH) Stock Could Be A Bargain On Cash Flow","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate-management-and-development/nyse-hhh/howard-hughes-holdings/news/howard-hughes-holdings-hhh-stock-could-be-a-bargain-on-cash","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794558235.468,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.894,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Howard Hughes Holdings (HHH) Leans Into Insurance As Valuation Stays In Focus","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https